{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Make cyberbullying a standalone criminal offence & raise mental health funding",
        "additional_details": "We call on the Government to legislate to make cyberbullying a standalone criminal offence and increase funding for mental health support to protect people online.\r\n \r\nThis petition is for the countless victims affected by online bullying. We want the Government to recognise that online bullying, which can be a contributing factor in suicide, is a serious public crisis \u2013 the Government must strengthen legislation, hold online platforms accountable and provide more funding for mental health support. No family should face a preventable loss.",
        "background": "Online bullying is 24/7, anonymous and inescapable for many, and can be a contributing factor in suicide. We believe it\u2019s a public health crisis with legal gaps. ",
